{"case_id": "dev-478915968e", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-01T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_7151574a2a13p", "author_id": "sim_author_907fb08321e7", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-01T12:00:00Z", "text": "After a month on the sidelines, I'm putting money to work in $ZYNTHO this week. The staking yield is steady and the unlock schedule is almost finished.", "text_sha256": "071a5bc8edfe7bfe0e3eee9c6d21d9f823b678f2adbcfedaa376e67c6c7fb9fe", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_97626998c490c3455ad8c17c", "source_id": "sim_post_7151574a2a13p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 151}]}
{"case_id": "dev-368352369e", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-02T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_6909d4fe546ap", "author_id": "sim_author_bfa1cf0b39b3", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-02T12:00:00Z", "text": "Of all the data-availability projects, $WOLKAR is where I want exposure right now. Fee revenue has grown for three straight quarters and the token still trades near its yearly low.", "text_sha256": "9c6e99689c6fe14a6f4ab5ee5ca0fb6f92063432600b710f5d1d9b2e41536a54", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_953a0feee1720f22f71da378", "source_id": "sim_post_6909d4fe546ap", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 180}]}
{"case_id": "dev-3a380392fd", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-03T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_fa5fa5e155e3p", "author_id": "sim_author_c5fee5abb009", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-03T12:00:00Z", "text": "Count me in on $XERBEL at these levels; I'm adding a starter position today.", "text_sha256": "bc4d4f9b86791787e64fc7f7f107a1d4873053f1486f3e8dc038d1608a498f40", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [{"source_id": "sim_post_e365a9631b04q", "author_id": "sim_author_5fe1d60586fd", "published_at_utc": "2025-04-03T00:00:00Z", "text": "Treasury proposal: the community fund should allocate part of its reserves to $XERBEL before the governance vote on Friday.", "text_sha256": "ca7510c8c5485d1288041640ee72e9076414fc6ac3a99851b5c04fc42c86a3ab", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_edd07592c4f0e1c756469b82", "source_id": "sim_post_fa5fa5e155e3p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 76}, {"evidence_id": "ev_dd5ea5b0e9a31b5c1f52d40d", "source_id": "sim_post_e365a9631b04q", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 123}]}
{"case_id": "dev-70258d9c4e", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-04T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_b35f3fbf0f1ep", "author_id": "sim_author_cc12d09f0fc1", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-04T12:00:00Z", "text": "Disclosure: this post is a paid partnership with the $YANDRO foundation. Separately from that arrangement, I've begun building a position in $YANDRO with my own funds and will keep adding in thirds over the next two weeks.", "text_sha256": "82fb2ac3e157aca854b794c13aad781c2918adfde2f68a5843d09aa71ecd7c13", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_86b30b7586cf73cb862e38c2", "source_id": "sim_post_b35f3fbf0f1ep", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 222}]}
{"case_id": "dev-126165126b", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-05T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_f8bb81df67f6p", "author_id": "sim_author_673a602c278d", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-05T12:00:00Z", "text": "Took a first bite of $CUSPEL this morning. If the market offers lower prices over the coming days, I plan to keep adding.", "text_sha256": "09c8249dc4ba8ab21dd7573b406e400773de6b98f7402d2ff36c98a58971882b", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_a5a1cfdb82d40b32a1232e74", "source_id": "sim_post_f8bb81df67f6p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 121}]}
{"case_id": "dev-955810196b", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-06T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_f7b26459f75ep", "author_id": "sim_author_4099bc86cd2e", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-06T12:00:00Z", "text": "Opened a long on $DROVAN perpetuals at the London open. Invalidation sits below last week's low, and I'm sizing small until the funding rate settles.", "text_sha256": "61493b983105fd683d0ab212ef5df581c00ffe4de60173d0d9aaebec09b3701c", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_3c0de78f44d7ebdc730776f5", "source_id": "sim_post_f7b26459f75ep", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 149}]}
{"case_id": "dev-8be4ac813d", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-07T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_1d60cd4ed234p", "author_id": "sim_author_c9760912a959", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-07T12:00:00Z", "text": "Trimmed $ESKILO after the run to new highs, and I'm rotating the proceeds into $FENWIK, which still trades at a deep discount to its peers.", "text_sha256": "3499543532af655d945e80c7a5d73e8d94aecde89e4533bae8a4fbe24b73d785", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_856ed6375ee8f2cf370c7210", "source_id": "sim_post_1d60cd4ed234p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 139}]}
{"case_id": "dev-0cf23e0829", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-08T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_abad8c295128p", "author_id": "sim_author_cb3f2b15bbf1", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-08T12:00:00Z", "text": "At these levels I'm a buyer of $GRUSOL. The market is pricing in a failed upgrade that the public testnet results simply do not support. Chart for reference.", "text_sha256": "2ca0f7aa89701aae4f89dad6796f6901f312274e64768c19b825072c1d5fb815", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [{"kind": "IMAGE", "reference": "https://example.invalid/im_a_buyer_of_missing_image/image"}], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_9dc78cda37263957799884c1", "source_id": "sim_post_abad8c295128p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 157}]}
{"case_id": "dev-2d54b8a78d", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-09T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_c1a7372ca21dp", "author_id": "sim_author_3ea7ae8e6d59", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-09T12:00:00Z", "text": "Back in $HAMBIK today. I sold everything in March, waited for the restructuring to complete, and the original thesis is intact again.", "text_sha256": "997697689bcd2587ae6565f9646d9592b78fade88ba2093f1b868c072ab5ca0d", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_562f2465caa61684e15eb4a5", "source_id": "sim_post_c1a7372ca21dp", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 133}]}
{"case_id": "dev-e56e67049e", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-10T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "author_id": "sim_author_6b6faf335a1e", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-10T12:00:00Z", "text": "Weekly allocation update:\n- Allocating to $IZTRON this week, roughly five percent of the book.\n- $JUBRAN: adding on weakness, with entries spread across the next few sessions.\n- $KESTOV: holding what I have, no new money going in.\nRisk notes follow in the thread.", "text_sha256": "3eeaac1f625315388c08927d66beca8291c568673659b10f9bebfa81c8a98811", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_62c3080272d7e4328d7be6e0", "source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 26}, {"evidence_id": "ev_f212ea86ea95616c7960d8ef", "source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 263}, {"evidence_id": "ev_44837fe79c1e9e6fba6b65ff", "source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "start_utf16": 26, "end_utf16": 95}, {"evidence_id": "ev_7190d56940edd05b2b04e8e6", "source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "start_utf16": 95, "end_utf16": 176}, {"evidence_id": "ev_3a2e481cde638ae50e5b12b0", "source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "start_utf16": 176, "end_utf16": 231}, {"evidence_id": "ev_15b3976824bd466d453ada63", "source_id": "sim_post_4dda27c4a6cep", "start_utf16": 231, "end_utf16": 263}]}
{"case_id": "dev-136939eebb", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-11T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_81f5f35e71bbp", "author_id": "sim_author_0ec550efedd7", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-11T12:00:00Z", "text": "Two entries I made today:\nStarted a position in $LAPRIN for the validator economics.\nPut fresh capital into $MURDOK on the treasury buyback news.\n$NOXELL stays on the watchlist until the audit is published.", "text_sha256": "33d2d478d33b9ee28bf1e729cb383a85f8844a270e8dc177a55185aa3586dbf5", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_ef5188ec88de3f7e83f8d8fa", "source_id": "sim_post_81f5f35e71bbp", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 26}, {"evidence_id": "ev_88eacc4f79ebc3c982489ea6", "source_id": "sim_post_81f5f35e71bbp", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 206}, {"evidence_id": "ev_b33005c51dc94a6e847715c9", "source_id": "sim_post_81f5f35e71bbp", "start_utf16": 26, "end_utf16": 85}, {"evidence_id": "ev_10b2ac34e4e7f54442bf76af", "source_id": "sim_post_81f5f35e71bbp", "start_utf16": 85, "end_utf16": 146}, {"evidence_id": "ev_7a67ead3c17baf178ecd0333", "source_id": "sim_post_81f5f35e71bbp", "start_utf16": 146, "end_utf16": 206}]}
{"case_id": "dev-1faab238f7", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-12T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_b1df34764191p", "author_id": "sim_author_01fd3c4254a1", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-12T12:00:00Z", "text": "This week was mostly travel. I spent three days at a developer meetup in Porto, where the main topic was account abstraction and how wallets should present signing requests to ordinary users. The best talk came from a small team that rebuilt their onboarding flow after watching twenty people fail to recover a seed phrase. Their conclusion was that the problem is not education but interface design, and I agree with them. On the train back I finished a long book about the history of clearing houses. It is dry in places, but the chapter on settlement failures in the nineteen-seventies explains a lot about why modern exchanges insist on collateral before anything else. I also recorded two podcast episodes. The first covers validator client diversity and why a single dominant client remains the largest systemic risk in most proof-of-stake networks. The second is a conversation with a researcher who studies sequencer decentralisation; we disagreed on timelines but agreed that shared sequencing is further away than most roadmaps suggest. Housekeeping notes: I rotated the keys on my hardware wallet, moved my notes app to an encrypted vault, and turned off the browser extension that kept asking for permissions it did not need. If you run a newsletter, please check your mailing provider settings, because several readers reported phishing emails that copied my formatting almost perfectly. For what it is worth, I am allocating a slice of new capital to $OBRANT this week, because the lending volumes there keep compounding while the token sits near the bottom of its range. Back to the week. The weather in Porto was grey but mild, and the coffee near the venue was excellent. Several attendees asked about the reading list I mentioned last month, so here it is again: a book on market microstructure, a short paper on fee markets, and an essay about governance capture in decentralised organisations. I will publish a longer review of the clearing-house book next week, together with a few thoughts on what it implies for on-chain settlement. Next month I am speaking at a smaller event in Ghent about wallet security for small teams. If you will be there, say hello; I will bring stickers and very strong opinions about multisig key ceremonies. Finally, thank you to everyone who answered last week's survey. Most of you want fewer price charts and more explanations of protocol mechanics, and that is the direction this newsletter will take for the rest of the year. The survey also showed that many of you read on a phone during a commute, so I will keep paragraphs short and avoid wide tables. As always, none of the travel or tooling mentioned here is sponsored, and I pay for my own conference tickets.", "text_sha256": "9e262105ca22943dcb267d54e2df4f923b9c3c2d85f2d513ccc50be8f4a67d4c", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_46116dc545fd90f953f79572", "source_id": "sim_post_b1df34764191p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 2721}]}
{"case_id": "dev-5b8ce82a20", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-13T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_1fc272f3c8eep", "author_id": "sim_author_b1af11cfa4c2", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-13T12:00:00Z", "text": "Buyers stepped in for $QUERIN right at the 200-day average, and on-chain data shows whales are buying in size, with three large wallets adding over the weekend. I'm watching this, not participating.", "text_sha256": "6e3f01b110a9ed57bf88c2dfca618ee480443c82654362d2c16bbfd7453b0d54", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_69b662f7229d190e8c43899f", "source_id": "sim_post_1fc272f3c8eep", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 198}]}
{"case_id": "dev-7edd470b9b", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-14T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_3ad1876f2b88p", "author_id": "sim_author_cd11d0fbb02b", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-14T12:00:00Z", "text": "I would have bought $SUNDEX below forty cents if I had been at my desk on Tuesday. Lesson noted, and I am not chasing it now.", "text_sha256": "5248a641113f990ef21db1df6870c667bcfe8fffd869331012dd293747e4f122", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_902bc0e0c847c820a3c1ac48", "source_id": "sim_post_3ad1876f2b88p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 125}]}
{"case_id": "dev-4bc47e3a81", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-15T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_ff51ff38d0c6p", "author_id": "sim_author_b61d13f130ec", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-15T12:00:00Z", "text": "I almost bought $TOVRIK yesterday, then the team postponed the mainnet launch again and I cancelled the order before it filled.", "text_sha256": "dfd1927e70056de89d0b943bf9899ec4783589dcd6cd82360d1c8479adf486ff", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_85b216bed17a2a43456581b6", "source_id": "sim_post_ff51ff38d0c6p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 127}]}
{"case_id": "dev-98bc92d21e", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-16T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_028a2370d4c4p", "author_id": "sim_author_83bce48860c6", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-16T12:00:00Z", "text": "A friend asked if he should buy $UMBRAX for his retirement account. I told him I don't give personal advice, and that I don't own any myself.", "text_sha256": "dff5e6028eb3167068e23392c96e78d84386448e67da9d0f0b9a64d6b3705101", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_b1114fbce5314b9153bb0d00", "source_id": "sim_post_028a2370d4c4p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 141}]}
{"case_id": "dev-6a2e445d92", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-17T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_9d0151a51807p", "author_id": "sim_author_0783ca394b6e", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-17T12:00:00Z", "text": "I like the people behind $VIDLOW, but I'm not a buyer of it here; the valuation already assumes flawless execution. And I'm never buying $WENTRA while insiders control seventy percent of the supply.", "text_sha256": "a800b4625a951443d502dc9084b3b63bebe0774d41fa7a7513dad48ae74b0848", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_450f5d27e6546f816d5a5a16", "source_id": "sim_post_9d0151a51807p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 198}]}
{"case_id": "dev-da24f0bacc", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-18T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_e72edc4794edp", "author_id": "sim_author_ec27c9d4fa05", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-18T12:00:00Z", "text": "Bought the dip in $XAPHON last year and I still hold every token. No additions planned for now.", "text_sha256": "ba43e88bf454a45010a34831f1d41753f9ac2d71e01dee54ded9bc4e999056ec", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_083276e36ff3829e5e7087cd", "source_id": "sim_post_e72edc4794edp", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 95}]}
{"case_id": "dev-e0e4ecd279", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-19T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_bb67f6711430p", "author_id": "sim_author_0ccba17136d7", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-19T12:00:00Z", "text": "$YOLMIR swept the buy-side liquidity above the range high and then reversed. Buy pressure has faded since the listing, so I expect a retest of the range midpoint before any trend resumes.", "text_sha256": "b297a248b8b60ba88e8d5a3dec43da49e87553d0b11ff1d7318840e7d336ca03", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_dbe82c451bfe0871c9ee28b5", "source_id": "sim_post_bb67f6711430p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 187}]}
{"case_id": "dev-3686664ebb", "synthetic": true, "available_at_utc": "2025-05-20T12:10:00Z", "primary": {"source_id": "sim_post_1bf4e7151c08p", "author_id": "sim_author_048b4d591c66", "published_at_utc": "2025-05-20T12:00:00Z", "text": "If I were you, I'd wait for $ARKOVA to reclaim the range before buying anything. Personally I'm staying flat until that happens.", "text_sha256": "5e7d31a7a0d25365803e69bf41c96a89abd775ac707afb90d2437f215ee7d74a", "capture_scope": "FULL_TEXT"}, "context": [], "unavailable_context": [], "asset_identity_evidence": [], "evidence_catalogue": [{"evidence_id": "ev_1f5982f8ac5c33b52d34e754", "source_id": "sim_post_1bf4e7151c08p", "start_utf16": 0, "end_utf16": 128}]}
